{"chunk_id": "00b6507772ed", "text": "Vasishtha refuses King Viswamitra\u2019s demand to exchange the divine cow Nandini even for a kingdom, explaining that she sustains sacred duties\u2014sacrifices, guests, and the gods. Enraged, Viswamitra attempts to seize the cow by force. Nandini, loyal to her sage, pleads for protection. Vasishtha, committed to forgiveness rather than violence, allows her to act if she wishes. The cow then manifests terrifying power: from different parts of her body emerge vast armies of many tribes that rout Viswamitra\u2019s forces without killing them. Witnessing this miracle, Viswamitra realizes that spiritual power surpasses royal might. Disgusted with Kshatriya strength, he renounces his kingdom and undertakes fierce asceticism, eventually attaining Brahmanhood. The episode illustrates a central theme of the epic: the superiority of spiritual discipline and inner power over worldly authority and military force.\nViswamitra tries to seize Vasishtha\u2019s divine cow Nandini, who magically defeats his army, leading Viswamitra to renounce kingship and pursue ascetic power.\nThemes: Brahmin vs Kshatriya power, asceticism vs force, divine cow Nandini, renunciation and transformation", "vector": [-0.012521849945187569, -0.02958841435611248, 0.010092542506754398, 0.01733269728720188, -0.01918879710137844, 0.01751011796295643, -0.029861370101571083, -0.03278199955821037, -0.00980593916028738, -0.03218149393796921, 0.010624806396663189, 0.018028734251856804, 0.011150246486067772, -0.0006043413304723799, -0.004039746709167957, 0.024142945185303688, 0.057812049984931946, -0.014029931277036667, 0.018192507326602936, -0.014084521681070328, -0.0016129985451698303, -0.00636328337714076, -0.006462229881435633, 0.01430288702249527, -0.007219682447612286, 0.013477195054292679, 0.012494553811848164, -0.02261439338326454, 0.004589070100337267, -0.030216213315725327, -0.010031127370893955, -0.007915719412267208, -0.0033368852455168962, -0.003028104081749916